// A stand-in for Apple's <metal_stdlib>, used only by ganbate-shader's tests to parse and
// type-check generated Metal Shading Language with a stock clang++ on any platform.
//
// It models the parts of MSL the generator emits: address-space and stage keywords (as
// nothing), vector types with Metal's sizes, alignments and swizzles (clang's
// ext_vector_type), matrices, packed vectors, textures, samplers and the built-in functions,
// with the same argument types as the Metal Shading Language Specification so that wrong
// types, arities and names fail to compile. Two differences from real MSL need a source
// rewrite before compiling (see tests/msl.rs): vector constructors such as
// `metal::float3(a, b)` are spelled `metal::make_float3(a, b)`, and a comparison of vectors
// yields an int vector, so `boolN` is an int vector here.
#pragma once

#include <stddef.h>
#include <type_traits>

